    "probe_text": "Here is the exact ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`. Despite the CLAUDE.md \"standard thin-controller\" framing, the real logic lives in Bean Validation, two `@InitBinder` `Validator`s, and a fleet of AOP aspects around `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Security (before anything)\n1. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Request-body validation & binding (`@Valid @RequestBody`)\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` (field by field):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n3. **`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice`** (`@InitBinder` Validator):\n   - Rejects blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`.\n   - **Side-effect (mutates DTO):** normalizes address via `StructuredAddress`/`AddressNormalizer` (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; composes `address` from line1/line2); rejects if resulting `address` is blank.\n   - **Side-effect (mutates DTO):** normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (assumes `+61` if no `+`, drops leading 0, 8\u201315 digits, national-length check); rejects if it can't.\n4. **`OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice`** (`@InitBinder` Validator): for known cities (Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane) enforces the region postcode range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown city or missing postcode is skipped.\n\n   *Any failure in phase 2 \u2192 400 ProblemDetail via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.*\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Pre-body aspect guards\n5. **`OwnerIdempotencyAdvice`** (`@Around`, highest precedence): if `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, returns the cached response as **200** and short-circuits everything below.\n6. **`OwnerDailyLimitAdvice`** (`@Before`): if \u2265 100 owners already registered for today's (business-day-adjusted) date \u2192 **429**.\n7. **`OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`** (`@Before`): if \u2265 50 owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409**. *(6 and 7 run in undefined order relative to each other.)*\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Controller body / persistence\n8. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)`** \u2014 field copy; invokes entity setters:\n   - `setRegistrationDate`: defaults null \u2192 today, then rolls to next business day (skips weekends + fixed 2026 holidays).\n   - `setEmail`: lower-cases.\n9. **`CustomerCode.of(...)`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `V2` + region + 2-digit fiscal year + 8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName) + Luhn check digit, with `-n` dedupe against existing codes. (Reads all owners via `findAllOwners`.)\n10. **`OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect`** (`@Before saveOwner`, new owners only): SHA-256 identity key over `telephone | lowercased email | soundex(lastName)`; if it matches any live owner \u2192 **409**.\n11. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** (`@Transactional` \u2014 the only write tx) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save`. Hibernate validates entity constraints, including `telephone` `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`; DB generates the id.\n12. **`CallMonitoringAspect`** times/counts each repository call (monitoring side-effect).\n13. **`AUDIT.info(\"owner created ...\")`** logged inline in the controller.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 `@AfterReturning` response enrichment & side-effects\nInnermost-first; `@Order`ed ones run last so they see fields set earlier:\n14. `OwnerSelfLinkAdvice` \u2192 sets `selfLink`.\n15. `OwnerCapacityWarningAdvice` \u2192 `capacityWarning=true` if city holds 40\u201349 owners.\n16. `OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice` \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning=true` if > 80 owners created today.\n17. `OwnerFiscalYearAdvice` \u2192 sets `fiscalYear`.\n18. `OwnerRiskFlagAdvice` \u2192 sets `riskFlag` (possible duplicate, disposable email domain, or city \u2265 40).\n19. `OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice` \u2192 sets `namesakeCount`, then `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel` (ceiling cap), and `ownerSegment`.\n20. `OwnerWelcomeNotifyAdvice` \u2192 logs a `WELCOME` line to `NOTIFY` (simulated email/notification).\n21. `OwnerCreateAuditAdvice` (`@Order(0)`) \u2192 writes the create audit line.\n22. `OwnerCreatedEventAdvice` (`@Order(-1)`, runs last) \u2192 publishes an `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event.\n23. `OwnerIdempotencyAdvice` caches the final response for the `Idempotency-Key`.\n24. Controller returns **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n**Notes:** There is no single request-wide transaction \u2014 `saveOwner` and each `findAllOwners` call are separate transactions. The aspect-thrown `429`/`409` are rendered by Spring's `ResponseStatusExceptionResolver`, not the `@ControllerAdvice`. The DTO fields `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` are never populated."
